// THE LLETYA ELVES. Five of them carry op3=Pickpocket in the cache - Goreu, Ysgawyn, Arvel,
// Mawrth and Kelyn - and the 2026-09-08 dead-op audit left them out on purpose: "they want their
// own rates and loot rather than citizen-tier". These are those rates.
//
// Level 85, 353.3 experience, a six second stun and 5 damage, and the loot table is the hero's
// with nature runes where his blood runes are: coins 280-350 at 105/128, two death runes at 8, a
// jug of wine at 6, three nature runes at 5, a fire orb at 2, a diamond at 1 and gold ore at 1.
//
// success_chance 15,99 puts the roll at 87/256 at level 85 and 100/256 at 99, which is the wiki's
// 33.94% and 39.2% - stat_random is (low*(99-L) + high*(L-1))/98 + 1 out of 256.
[pickpocket_elf]
table=pickpocket
data=npc,mourning_town_elf_1
data=npc,mourning_town_elf_2
data=npc,mourning_town_elf_3
data=npc,mourning_town_elf_4
data=npc,mourning_town_elf_5
data=level,85
data=experience,3533
data=stun_ticks,10
data=stun_damage,5
data=success_chance,15,99
data=loot,coins,280,350,105
data=loot,deathrune,2,2,8
data=loot,jug_wine,1,1,6
data=loot,naturerune,3,3,5
data=loot,fire_orb,1,1,2
data=loot,diamond,1,1,1
data=loot,gold_ore,1,1,1
data=pocket,elf's pocket

// THE MASTER FARMERS. Reported as "master farmer's not coded for pickpocketing": all three carry
// op3=Pickpocket and pickpocket.rs2 has had the triggers for them all along, so the click reached
// ~attempt_pick_pocket, found no row here, and said "Nothing interesting happens."
//
// "Level 38 Thieving is required to pickpocket them. Successful pickpockets can result in most
// types of seeds, excluding tree seeds and fruit tree seeds. 43 Thieving experience is granted
// upon successfully pickpocketing a Master Farmer. Failing to pickpocket a Master Farmer results
// in being stunned for five seconds and taking three hitpoints of damage."
// (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Master_Farmer). success_chance is the wiki's own skilling
// success chart for this target: low=90, high=240 at 38 Thieving.
//
// THE WEIGHTS ARE OUT OF 10000, not 128 - see loot_total in the dbtable, which exists because this
// table's rarest seed is one in nine thousand and cannot be written as a whole number of 128ths.
// They are the wiki's rarities turned into ten-thousandths, and the six sub-table totals it states
// are what they add up to:
//
//   allotments 4852 (485/1000)   bushes   971 (97/1000)
//   hops       2431 (243/1000)   special   49 (5/1000)
//   flowers    1220 (122/1000)   herbs    477 (48/1000)
//
// FOUR SEEDS ARE NOT IN THIS CACHE and their weight stays in the sub-table it came from, so the
// proportions above hold: snape grass (1/260) goes to the potato seed, poison ivy (1/937) to the
// redberry, and the seaweed and potato cactus spores to the mushroom. The herb table's rounding
// remainder goes to the guam. Left unassigned, that weight would be a successful pickpocket that
// paid nothing, which is a thing the live game never does.
//
// NOT MODELLED: in the live game the herb seeds' rarity scales with Farming level up to 85. The
// loot column is a flat weight with nowhere to put a second rate, so these are the BASE figures -
// what an unscaled player gets - which is also what a 2006-era server should be giving, since the
// scaling was added in 2019 to stop low-stat bots farming them.
[pickpocket_master_farmer]
table=pickpocket
data=npc,master_farmer_1
data=npc,master_farmer_2
data=npc,martin_the_master_farmer
data=level,38
data=experience,430
data=stun_ticks,8
data=stun_damage,3
data=success_chance,90,240
// allotments - 4852, the potato carrying the snape grass seed this cache has not got
data=loot,potato_seed,1,4,1808
data=loot,onion_seed,1,3,1328
data=loot,cabbage_seed,1,3,694
data=loot,tomato_seed,1,2,637
data=loot,sweetcorn_seed,1,2,221
data=loot,strawberry_seed,1,1,111
data=loot,watermelon_seed,1,1,53
// hops - 2431
data=loot,barley_seed,1,12,556
